<title>PARAGUAY: Paraguay to receive $200 mln agricultural loan.</title>
<headline>Paraguay to receive $200 mln agricultural loan.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION, Paraguay 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paraguayan government on Tuesday said it would receive a $200 million loan from Germany's Dresdner Bank AG to boost agriculture.</p>
<p>The three-year loan, which is subject to congressional approval, will carry a nominal annual interest rate of 7.9 percent, Government Planning Secretary Guillermo Sosa said at a news conference.</p>
<p>It would target a credit-line plan for small agricultural producers and agricultural exports such as cotton, he said. ((- Jose Maria Amarilla, Asuncion Newsroom +595 21 444527))</p>
